1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,594
Last time, the quest paid by itself,

2
00:00:03,044 --> 00:00:05,577
and the call afterward was just manners.

3
00:00:06,477 --> 00:00:09,674
Today the quest isn't over until the crew reports in.

4
00:00:10,574 --> 00:00:11,556
And when they do,

5
00:00:12,006 --> 00:00:13,846
a second voice comes on the line.

6
00:00:15,646 --> 00:00:18,566
Along the way you'll learn which call sits on top,

7
00:00:19,016 --> 00:00:20,443
which ships get called,

8
00:00:20,893 --> 00:00:23,710
and what Comms can do with a call that's waiting.

9
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:26,865
Here's the new step in the Quest Log,

10
00:00:27,315 --> 00:00:28,898
with Chief Ives under its order,

11
00:00:29,348 --> 00:00:31,972
and an order that sends the crew to Comms.

12
00:00:33,772 --> 00:00:35,229
I start with the quest before it.

13
00:00:36,129 --> 00:00:37,805
I take its reward off,

14
00:00:38,255 --> 00:00:41,161
and I point its Then line at a new key.

15
00:00:42,061 --> 00:00:45,144
Then I replace the beat below it with a quest.

16
00:00:46,944 --> 00:00:48,318
Look at what's different.

17
00:00:49,218 --> 00:00:52,462
There's no Beat line, so the crew will see it in the Quest Log.

18
00:00:53,362 --> 00:00:55,984
There's an objective, which sends them to Comms.

19
00:00:56,884 --> 00:00:58,470
The reward has moved here.

20
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:01,892
The Action lines are the same two as before,

21
00:01:02,342 --> 00:01:04,772
because Action works on any quest.

22
00:01:06,572 --> 00:01:09,626
And look at what's missing: there's no Done when.

23
00:01:10,526 --> 00:01:13,502
Nothing in the game finishes this step by itself.

24
00:01:15,302 --> 00:01:17,809
The description belongs to Chief Ives,

25
00:01:18,259 --> 00:01:20,030
because the ledger is his.

26
00:01:20,930 --> 00:01:24,139
So it opens with his face, copied from his record.

27
00:01:25,039 --> 00:01:27,894
Then it tells the crew why they have to say it out loud.

28
00:01:28,794 --> 00:01:30,463
The objective gives the order,

29
00:01:30,913 --> 00:01:33,104
and the description gives the reason.

30
00:01:34,304 --> 00:01:36,686
So what does finish it?

31
00:01:37,136 --> 00:01:38,524
An answer from the crew does.

32
00:01:39,424 --> 00:01:41,124
Here's the call on Comms now.

33
00:01:41,574 --> 00:01:43,866
Quill is asking, not congratulating,

34
00:01:44,316 --> 00:01:46,435
and the crew has one answer.

35
00:01:47,335 --> 00:01:48,610
So I change her lines,

36
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:52,188
and on the crew's answer, after the semicolon,

37
00:01:52,638 --> 00:01:55,236
I write completes, and the step's key.

38
00:01:57,036 --> 00:02:00,099
Now here's the rule for a call that a step is waiting on.

39
00:02:00,999 --> 00:02:04,318
Every answer that ends the call has to finish the step.

40
00:02:05,218 --> 00:02:07,213
If I add an answer that just hangs up,

41
00:02:07,663 --> 00:02:11,390
the call is gone, and the step stays in the Quest Log for good.

42
00:02:12,290 --> 00:02:13,634
And lint can't see that.

43
00:02:14,834 --> 00:02:17,522
A call can have more than one person on the line.

44
00:02:18,422 --> 00:02:20,822
On Comms, I press Continue,

45
00:02:21,272 --> 00:02:24,844
and the face and the name change to Chief Ives.

46
00:02:25,744 --> 00:02:28,643
Chief Ives has been in my cast since Lecture 2,

47
00:02:29,093 --> 00:02:30,580
with nothing to say.

48
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,801
So I give him a block:

49
00:02:33,251 --> 00:02:36,366
an at sign, his key, and two takes of his own.

50
00:02:38,166 --> 00:02:39,976
The call still belongs to Quill,

51
00:02:40,426 --> 00:02:42,428
and it's her name on the list.

52
00:02:43,328 --> 00:02:44,813
But inside the call,

53
00:02:45,263 --> 00:02:48,016
each block brings its own name and its own face.

54
00:02:48,916 --> 00:02:52,960
Remember that the line is an at sign and a key, and nothing else.

55
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:56,369
Write his full name there, and his block is gone,

56
00:02:56,819 --> 00:02:58,611
and lint says clean.

57
00:02:59,811 --> 00:03:02,894
Calls wait in a list, and the newest one is on top.

58
00:03:03,794 --> 00:03:07,186
So a call that matters can get pushed down by a later one.

59
00:03:08,086 --> 00:03:09,662
A call never times out,

60
00:03:10,112 --> 00:03:11,935
and only one is open at a time.

61
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:17,051
To keep a call on top, I give its scene a priority.

62
00:03:17,951 --> 00:03:20,238
A higher number sits above a lower one,

63
00:03:20,688 --> 00:03:23,943
and a call with no priority counts as zero.

64
00:03:24,843 --> 00:03:27,539
Use it for a call that a step is waiting on,

65
00:03:27,989 --> 00:03:29,325
and leave the others alone.

66
00:03:30,525 --> 00:03:32,790
I've never said which ship she calls,

67
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,323
and I don't have to,

68
00:03:34,773 --> 00:03:37,767
because every player ship is called.

69
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:40,849
With one ship, that's all there is to it.

70
00:03:42,649 --> 00:03:45,570
With two, each ship gets its own copy of the call.

71
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:48,766
But the quest is shared, so there's only one of it.

72
00:03:49,666 --> 00:03:52,778
One crew says yes, and it starts for everybody.

73
00:03:53,678 --> 00:03:57,466
And the first crew to report gets the side paid, just once.

74
00:03:59,266 --> 00:04:02,156
So write your lines for any ship that might hear them,

75
00:04:02,606 --> 00:04:06,108
and keep quests like this for missions flown by one ship.

76
00:04:07,308 --> 00:04:09,806
This part has nothing to type.

77
00:04:10,706 --> 00:04:14,071
It's what the person at Comms can do with what you wrote,

78
00:04:14,521 --> 00:04:16,599
and all of it is on the Comms console.

79
00:04:17,499 --> 00:04:19,351
They can leave a call waiting,

80
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:20,775
they can open it,

81
00:04:21,225 --> 00:04:22,489
and they can press Back.

82
00:04:23,389 --> 00:04:26,395
There's a drop-down that chooses where the conversation is drawn:

83
00:04:26,845 --> 00:04:30,426
both, the main screen, this console, or off.

84
00:04:31,326 --> 00:04:34,014
Every finished call gets a row under the Hails tab,

85
00:04:34,464 --> 00:04:36,235
by the name of who called.

86
00:04:37,135 --> 00:04:40,954
And the ship's log gets a line that says what the crew answered.

87
00:04:42,754 --> 00:04:45,026
So an answer is a decision the crew makes once.

88
00:04:45,926 --> 00:04:49,016
Everything else on Comms lets them put it off.

89
00:04:50,216 --> 00:04:52,621
Lint names ten mistakes in this lecture,

90
00:04:53,071 --> 00:04:54,565
and the page lists them.

91
00:04:55,465 --> 00:04:57,387
These two it can't see.

92
00:04:58,287 --> 00:05:02,473
If I take the completes off the answer, lint says clean,

93
00:05:02,923 --> 00:05:04,805
and the step can never be finished.

94
00:05:06,605 --> 00:05:09,848
And if I leave the Beat line in, lint says clean again.

95
00:05:10,748 --> 00:05:12,475
The step still works and pays,

96
00:05:12,925 --> 00:05:14,977
but the crew is never told to report.

97
00:05:15,877 --> 00:05:18,489
So check both of those with your own eyes.

98
00:05:19,689 --> 00:05:20,665
Let's play it through.

99
00:05:21,565 --> 00:05:24,351
I take the quest, the way we did last time.

100
00:05:25,251 --> 00:05:27,929
Thirty seconds later the beacon is set,

101
00:05:28,379 --> 00:05:31,175
and there's my new step, telling me to report.

102
00:05:32,075 --> 00:05:33,349
And there's the call.

103
00:05:35,149 --> 00:05:36,399
It opens on Quill,

104
00:05:36,849 --> 00:05:40,001
and when I press Continue, that's Chief Ives.

105
00:05:40,901 --> 00:05:44,944
I press Back, and the call waits, and so does the step.

106
00:05:45,844 --> 00:05:49,001
I open it again, and this time I give the answer.

107
00:05:49,901 --> 00:05:53,047
The step is done, and now the quest has paid.

108
00:05:54,247 --> 00:05:57,486
Now it's your turn: put more voices on your calls.

109
00:05:58,386 --> 00:06:00,160
Give Ives a block in the first call,

110
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:02,784
and let Captain Sable listen in on the offer.

111
00:06:03,684 --> 00:06:07,448
Then break the report on purpose, and watch what lint doesn't say.

112
00:06:09,248 --> 00:06:12,231
Next time, a side that remembers what the crew did.
